We walk down toward the beach together.
It is nine o'clock, but the sky is still light.
I look up at the beautiful colors.
"The sun has not gone down at all yet," I say to Nina.
I think back to my first month here.
"In January it was completely dark at four in the afternoon," I explain.
"I stood at the bus stop every day after work."
"I was freezing, and I waited for the bus in the dark."
Nina smiles at me.
"Yes, the Danish winter was very long," she answers.
"But now the summer has finally arrived."
We have walked for a quarter of an hour now.
Now we can see the water between the trees.
"You have made it through your first winter," Nina says happily.
I nod and take a deep breath.
I came here in the dark.
But now I have almost forgotten the cold.
Tonight, everything is bright and beautiful.
